{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance","id":990737,"title":"Post Your Durance!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-20T18:38:37-07:00","id":990737,"title":"Post Your Durance!","content":"The Durance is one of the coolest parts of CtL, but it's something that sometimes people have trouble with, so why not have a thread where we can post Durances, either ones our characters have or just ideas? <br /> <br /> Brittany Martin always loved fantasy. Fantasy novels, Dungeons and Dragons, fairy tales, anything else like that. Her favorite pastime was to walk in the woods behind her house and dream she was in a faraway land, on some adventure. But as the years wore on, she had to realize that the world had little time for fantasies. So she found herself walking in the woods once again on her seventeenth birthday, desperate to escape from the college application process, out for one final burst of fantasy. And that was when the Lady approached her, riding out of the forest on her noble steed. She offered Brittany adventures beyond her wildest dreams in a faraway land, the chance to become a hero. She's lost things from her memory, but she can never forget that she went willingly, no matter how much she wishes she could. <br /> <br /> Beautiful as the Lady's domain was, Brittany wasn't particularly prepared to be a knight. Playing D&amp;D doesn't prepare you for having all the bones in your leg smashed by the troll you were sent to hunt. But she just barely triumphed, and managed to limp back from her first &quot;quest&quot; to have the bones painfully regrown by a &quot;healing potion&quot;. Quest after quest passed, and each time Brittany nearly died but managed to triumph and drag herself back. She gradually improved, learning swordplay and riding and growing stronger and faster. It was painful and dangerous, but she was living out her fantasies, wasn't she? Who cares if she spent an entire month in agony while her skin and organs grew back after being immolated in the death spasms of the first dragon she killed? And killing dragons got easier. And that was enough to make her ignore the peasants laboring to death in the Lady's fields or the chained servants doing her bidding. Speaking of ignoring, while the Lady lavished praise and attention on her at first, she became more and more distant. She lost interest in Brittany. She found more knights. Soon, her quests were delivered by messengers and not the Lady herself. <br /> <br /> The quests got easier, though. Not just because she got better, but because the Lady found new jobs for her. Catching runaways, keeping her gladiators in line, putting down peasant revolts...by that time, she was so absorbed into her role that she didn't question it. That was, until she saw the old man. She hadn't seen the Lady for months. No dragons has attacked the kingdom lately. It was just a routine job: hunt down a &quot;traitor to the kingdom&quot;. So she rode out after the escaped servant, chasing him long and hard until she finally came to the wall of thorns around the kingdom. She dismounted her house at the edge of a vast lake and approached him, and he simply knelt down before her and waited. She raised her sword, and looked into his eyes, and that was when it all came down. The sight of the man's wizened, desperate face finally broke through the years of conditioning. She looked away, to the lake, and the noble knight saw the features of a dragon upon her face: scales, a forked tongue, and curling horns. She ran for the thorns, pushing through them, the pain no obstacle as she made her escape. <br /> <br /> Now, she works as a Summer Court mercenary. The fervor with which she attacks the Gentry and her servants is the only thing she's found that gives her a reprieve from the guilt.<br /> <br /> Brittany &quot;Britomart&quot; Martin is a tall woman with an athletic build, slicked-back bleached blonde hair, and perfectly bronzed skin, though she tends to carry herself in a rather nervous, edgy manner. In her Mien, she has black, pointed nails, reptilian pupils, a forked tongue, and spiraling horns coming from her head. When she Embraces the Wyrd, her horns grow longer, her teeth turn into black fangs, and her nails lengthen to slightly curved claws. A reptilian tail grows from her back, and wings of flame and ash ignite on her shoulders. Her clothing is replaced with armor that looks as if it was once gleaming gold, but is now rusted and webbed with numerous cracks from which steam rises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-21-2016, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T19:39:00-07:00","id":990761,"title":"","content":"Lionheart was stolen out of reality to fight in an endless medieval fantasy war for a cruel Keeper's amusement, with two armies made of enslaved hobs and kidnapped Lost eternally clashing and dying in the muck of a battlefield of a forgotten legend. He realized that this conflict would never end, that more people would be taken in order to fight and die without purpose, and instead rallied both armies under his banner; if they would die here, then let it be in a glorious, suicidal charge against their tormentor, rather than pointlessly killing each other. Deals were made, oaths were sworn, final speeches given, and as the two sides met on the bloody plain and began their doomed assault... he fled. The screams of the soldiers who'd united in his name echoed in his ears as he abandoned them, their last act of defiance easily masking his escape, and he returned to reality wounded far deeper by guilt than by any blade or Thorn. <br /> <br /> (Lionheart later went on to join the Summer Court and rise to its throne before militarizing the freehold and readying them for open war against a bloody Charlatan in an attempt to redeem himself by successfully dying in battle in another suicidal battle; he was killed by his motleymates who saw no point in leading an entire freehold to ruin in order to assuage one man's shame.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T20:58:17-07:00","id":990784,"title":"","content":"August spent his durance as part of a group of changelings who are forced to shapechange over and over and be NPC's for their Gentries attempts at mastering the relatively new storytelling medium of codified roleplaying games, and two of the rules are that PC's can leave whenever they wish and if a PC is killed they will remain dead until the party members choose to resurrect them.<br /> <br /> This gave him the opportunity to be what he always wanted to be, do things he could only dream of... but he had no choice of which thing he'll be each day. He got to do fantastic things and he cannot deny that he enjoyed many of the times he had in his durance... but dying hundreds of times, being forced to be something he isn't, having to act opposite to every part of your personality just because that's what the story needs today, having to do horrible things because today the gamesmaster decided you'll be a villain... He couldn't take or deal with that for an eternity.<br /> <br /> In the end, August eventually was used as skilled assassin NPC allowing him to get the drop on a PC who had left the group for some scouting. Just as he was about to kill the Gentry PC he had ambushed he stops and instead searches the helpless PC, quickly finding his character sheet. Immediately, he takes on the role of that PC, defying his place as an NPC. But instead of immediately leaving as is his new found rights would allow, he instead decides to continue the adventure and begins fighting his fellow party members, purposely putting them in positions so that the other NPC's can take the character sheets too. He was able to defeat three of the PC's before he decided he'd have to leave or die himself.<br /> <br /> He is now Mirrorskin/Fairest courtier of the Sand Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T02:37:25-07:00","id":990872,"title":"","content":"Here's mine:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://hydra-media.cursecdn.com/pillarsofeternity.gamepedia.com/c/cb/Durance-portrait.jpg?version=8ad8c27801a58ca643a9ef76dc052984\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T07:28:11-07:00","id":990945,"title":"","content":"I actually though a duranced based on Bedazzled with Liz Hurly would be cool, but with my own twists.<br /> <br /> This is inspired by Bedazzled not complete recreation of it below.<br /> <br /> Character has a crush on a beautiful woman he keeps seeing in his dreams, someone who keeps meeting briefly at work, but while friendly and polite, she doesn't really notice him.<br /> <br /> In a moment of lonely dispair while by himself he whispers he'd give his soul to be with her.<br /> <br /> <br /> His future Keeper hears this, and appears in the room, appearing ravishing. She introduces herself as the Supreme Devil of Unspeakable Desires and that she's come to deal for his soul.<br /> <br /> She offers him three wishes and he makes them all on the spot. He wishes to have the power to seduce women, he wishes to be rich and he wishes to be powerful.<br /> <br /> The Devil tells him to follow her into the Hedge and he does, the thorn rip at him, but he continues until there is a a flash, and he appears in a Palace, his Palace, with the girl from his dreams on his arm.<br /> <br /> Sadly the Kingdom he rules is at war and hours after arriving and bedding his wife, his Palace is swarming with enemies and the Palace is burning and his own wife is carried off screaming by lusty raiders as a prize of war.<br /> <br /> He calls for the Devil and she comes and agrees to try again at granting his wish right and a flash of light, and he's in a gorgeous chateau in the Alps with with the woman from his dreams and her Olympic Snowboarding team joining him in his Chateau to wait out the storm.<br /> <br /> Everything is perfect, he's playfully seducing the snow boarders until the Chateau of his gets hit by an avalche.<br /> <br /> He calls out out for the devil just as it hits and a flash and he's now in a tropical paradise sipping drinks and chilling on a nude beach, when just as things get interesting, a massive shark arrives and starts eating swimmers.<br /> <br /> He calls for the devil again and this continues with each fantasy going horrifically wrong.<br /> <br /> Eventually he's like enough, enough!<br /> <br /> But the Devil tells him a deal is a deal, and that she has already claimed his soul, along with the rest of him, so things continue.<br /> <br /> Eventually he realizes that the devil kept her word to him about making him a great seducer, which she did by making his touch sexually charged and hypnotic.<br /> <br /> So he uses it on her and finds out that there is a special rite (her taboo) that when done summons her and allows the summoner to command her.<br /> <br /> He also learns she's not really a devil, she's a fae and he learns he vice, virtue, greatest aspiration, ect...<br /> <br /> He betrays her trust and uses the rite and then demands she set him free which she does, abit pouting.<br /> <br /> She tells him one more thing, which really pisses him off. The woman from his dreams, woman is his huntsman, that she stalked his dream as bait, creating false memories of them meeting, and leaving hints that he should offer his soul for her, and that now that he's escaped, she'll be hunting him to return his soul to the rightful owner.<br /> <br /> Having betrayed the trust of the Devil, who he now just calls Liz, who had turned him into a Dearheart when she granted his wish, that betrayal transformed him into a Darkling, although he only knows that because she explained it too him.<br /> <br /> He remembers the rite which he uses to enslaved his former Keeper, just revenge as far as he's concerned (Farie Favour merit, which he reinvests by preparing the rite again after using it).<br /> <br /> He's always on the look out for the woman from his dreams, the huntsman who tricked him fearing and yearning for her at the same time.<br /> <br /> This oddly close relationship has freaked many fellow members of his Freehold, but no one wants to fuck with someone who can enslave his Keeper, even to a limited degree, so no one fucks with him and they're even polite to him, at least to his face, but rumours and talk abound about him, suggesting he's a loyalist.<br /> <br /> For his Keepers part, she finds it all to be a fun game and is oddly amused by being his slave and she very flirty with everyone around her, very naughty.<br /> <br /> His mien is he has glowing red eyes, horns, and a massive floating Grimoire that is actually his heart.<br /> <br /> Part of the rite to control his Keeper involved cutting his own heart out, magically turning the still beating heart into a Grimiore and writing the rite inside of it, which he did in her domain (which is why it didn't kill him).<br /> <br /> Hitting the Grimiore does it no damage, not even a scratch, to damage it, one has to stab the empty cavity where his heart used to lay. This severs the link between him and his heart killing him (effectly its akin to stabbing someone in the heart).<br /> <br /> All his contracts, pledges, his Keepers rite, his Mantle, and the secrets he gains via his kith blessing are all contained in his Heart/Grimiore, written in his blood, which has the title Heart of Betrayal embossed in Gold letters on the black leather cover.<br /> <br /> It smells faintly of blood and leaks shadows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-21-2016, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:59:37-07:00","id":991034,"title":"","content":"Another character I'm working on was used as a living instrument of arson by a crooked Fae businessman with a sun for a head. Phoebus works by offering people increasingly expensive deals, then offering them &quot;odd jobs&quot; to pay off the debt, which, of course, only ever gets deeper. One way he does this is by giving them dangerous jobs involving sabotaging his various rivals in Arcadia and expecting them to pay for potions and tools to complete them (or regrow any limbs they lost doing them), and of course he's happy to give you a loan to buy that new sword. With interest, of course. He's not running a charity. She was sent to burn buildings for him, and he talked her into buying an &quot;elixir&quot; that would &quot;improve her performance&quot;, which was what made her a Fireheart. He is unfailingly polite, and no matter what criminal enterprise or scam he's involved in, he remains absolutely certain that he is a legitimate and upstanding businessman. Calling this into question is best not done, as it is the only thing that can make him lose his temper.<br /> <br /> She has bright red metallic skin and orange gemstone eyes. Her body seems plastic and flexible, shape and mass usually shifting slightly. Rope fuses encircle her, forming patterns that look like muscles growing outside her body. Her skin is embedded with shiny black lumps that ignite when she's excited or using her powers. When she Embraces the Wyrd, the black clusters warp into exhaust pipes that constantly vent smoke and flame. Her fuses light and rip free of her body, flailing around her like tails. Her flexible flesh hardens and reshapes itself, giving her a large, imposing appearance with wide, artificially spherical shoulders and hands. The smells of smoke and chemicals permeate the area around her, and bits of the environment spontaneously catch fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-21-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:53:41-07:00","id":991137,"title":"","content":"Were's the durence in Arcadia for her or did she do the jobs for him in Arcadia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:04:01-07:00","id":991213,"title":"","content":"Can you post here if you want help fleshing out your Durance? Because I basically have a character that's pretty well-defined post and pre-Durance, but I'm having trouble with his durance.<br /> <br /> I know a lot about how he got into the Durance, though. He was a foster kid, always moving from one home to the next for as long as he can remember. He was the kid who everyone said looked shifty, or dangerous, or lazy or any number of other stereotypes. To survive that kind of life, you have to be the perfect kid, obedient and a good worker. Problem was, he never really could pull that off. Inevitably, the foster &quot;parents&quot; replaced him with other, cuter children; or he punched another kid after they made fun of his old clothes and his bad grades (not his fault he'd switched school districts halfway through the first semester); or he just ran away when the home situation got dangerous. It was not what anyone would call a happy childhood, but as he walked down the streets on the day before his 19th birthday, he could only think about how much worse it was going to be on the streets. He had a high school degree, the clothes on his back, a backpack, a phone and a little bag of all the money he'd saved over the years, but he didn't have a bank account or the credit to get a loan on an apartment. He was going to be on the streets. <br /> <br /> And this is where I kinda get lost and stuck. I have a concept for his Keeper, but not fleshed out. And I have little idea how he got caught or got out. I just have the concept of a bunch of Keepers who think of humans in the way that the worst of European missionaries thought of the native populations they &quot;ministered&quot; to. They are horrified by our primitive &quot;normality&quot; and see it as their duty to teach us civilization, otherwise known as the alien logic of faerie. So they're running a sort of Victorian Domby Hall/Work House Domain, but without any regard for Euclidean geometry or the laws of time and it's trying to teach you that you should be ashamed of thinking that gravity pulls you down instead of pushing you purple or just doing whatever the hell I want it to do. <br /> <br /> Drew a blank on how he escapes, but his post-durance life is where i started the character, so I know this part very well. His durance has stunted his growth and made him mentally a grizzled old cigar-smoking, hard-drinking noir detective, but forever physically stuck in the body of a child. With makeup and a fake beard, he can convince the gullibe for a little bit, but he supernaturally exudes this aura of &quot;help this poor baby&quot;. He makes money doing the kind of things private detectives in real life actually do, usually finding dirt on shady husbands or looking for runaway kids. He never meets the clients, doing all his business through a site that he's promoted as an urban legend through various fake accounts on various forums. But if you really need to find someone who doesn't want to be found, you come to him. <br /> <br /> I forget his name, but it was just a silly placeholder at the moment. In terms of appearance, he doesn't look majorly inhuman, but everything he wears immediately becomes dirty and ragged and he always looks like he's just been beaten. I was toying with making his mien be a constantly crying child with clothes made of his tears when I was considering making him an elemental, but then the concept changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:22:57-07:00","id":991221,"title":"","content":"That's a very interesting concept. I'd guess Wizened or maybe even Fairest? It honestly seems like you have most of his arc quite well fleshed out. You have a good concept for the Durance, do you need help working out what happened during it and how it changed him? The &quot;non-Euclidean Victorian workhouse&quot; idea is already a really strong image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:19:37-07:00","id":991264,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's a really striking Durance. Do you have an idea for what Kith he's supposed to wind up as? You've got most of the idea there, but figuring out what he'd be turned into reflects pretty heavily on what his Keeper is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:38:36-07:00","id":991271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=991264#post991264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's a really striking Durance. Do you have an idea for what Kith he's supposed to wind up as? You've got most of the idea there, but figuring out what he'd be turned into reflects pretty heavily on what his Keeper is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might suggest my conversion of the Drudge kith. But if we're sticking with canon kiths, maybe one of the crafting kiths like Artist, Maker, and Smith?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T21:41:05-07:00","id":991272,"title":"","content":"Hm, you'd have to work in some sort of crafting angle for those to work. The updated 2e kith has an investigation-themed Kith called the &quot;Slewfoot&quot;, so maybe look into that? But Drudge or Chatelaine could also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T08:52:18-07:00","id":991408,"title":"","content":"My initial concept was just the humor/strategy potential of manipulating people's reactions to children, both those whose instinct is to help and those whose instinct is to hurt. I actually got someone to write up a homebrew kith for it in the Changeling Kiths thread a while back called the Orphanwretch. I'll post it when I have more time.<br /> <br /> So yeah, you're right, I do have more figured out then I realized. I'm just not sure how he escaped and the process of the change, and that means that I'm both missing part of his motivation and, depending on the edition I end up playing him in, his Seeming. I was initially interested in him being a Grimm, but as I looked into it, it felt too limiting ironically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T11:06:33-07:00","id":991456,"title":"","content":"My Ifrit was a stereotypical deal with the devil, sold their &quot;soul,&quot; ended up in Hell and had to eventually get sent to reality as a Loyalist to recruit more people for the Devil through deals. Went all Darkling and broke away by backstabbery, and is now on the run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T14:54:49-07:00","id":991537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=991456#post991456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Ifrit was a stereotypical deal with the devil, sold their &quot;soul,&quot; ended up in Hell and had to eventually get sent to reality as a Loyalist to recruit more people for the Devil through deals. Went all Darkling and broke away by backstabbery, and is now on the run.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> NIce. Have you figured out how he got away, or is he not sure himself yet due to good Clarity obscuring his Arcadian memories?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869958#post869958\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869958#post869958\"> Changeling Kiths (2E) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869958#post869958\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/841149-changeling-kiths-2e?p=869958#post869958 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Here are some conversions of several kiths from both the 1E Changeling supplements (like Winter Masques and Night Horrors: Grim Fears) and the homebrew that's lying </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Here's the kith I asked White Oak Dragon to write up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T05:03:06-07:00","id":991808,"title":"","content":"Literally backstabbing their immediate boss with an iron knife she picked up on a job. Iron does wonders in Faerie. Still has the scars from hiding it under her clothes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T11:18:05-07:00","id":994121,"title":"","content":"Is this thread dead? That's too bad. It was really interesting. A good source of inspiration too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T16:47:06-07:00","id":994284,"title":"","content":"An artist and musician whose durance was not unlike the tale of Arachne in Greek mythology: his jealous Keeper transformed him into a spider and set him loose to spend what remained of his life endlessly spinning webs to survive in the gardens beyond the thorns. Only when he remembered his former life and lulled his Keeper to sleep with music by plucking the threads of his web did he finally have a chance to escape. Wizened Skitterskulk/Steepscrambler who now makes a living as a busker, street artist and, among the Freehold, crafter of tokens and hedgespun items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T18:31:04-07:00","id":994314,"title":"","content":"I like it. A classic Durance, but in a mythical way. What made you decide to make him Wizened instead of a Beast though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T20:25:00-07:00","id":994368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=994121#post994121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this thread dead? That's too bad. It was really interesting. A good source of inspiration too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Threads can have lulls. Four days is not weird as a lull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T01:36:38-07:00","id":994462,"title":"","content":"I'll be posting soon some details on the durance of that Grimm Spelldrinker concept I did for a detective crossover thread made by Vent0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T07:16:38-07:00","id":994555,"title":"","content":"She was a star in her hayday. Directors and producers used to clamor to get her to grace their Broadway stages. She was beautiful, elegant, had a voice that could bring tears to the audiences eyes. But that was then. Now, she's older, not as beautiful. Her voice doesn't command the wonder it used to. Now she has to take whatever parts she can get. It's not that she doesn't have skill, she's just past her prime, and for a woman like her, that's heartbreaking.<br /> <br /> She was on stage at some off-broadway production. It wasn't big, it wasn't the lead, but it was the best she could do when the only role available for someone her age was somebody's mother. The play finished she went to her dressing room when someone came in. He was a man about her age, handsome, with salt and pepper hair and an air of confidence. He told her she was the best thing on that stage, told her it was a tragedy that she had been pushed aside the way she had. They went to dinner and they talked. Eventually, the man admitted he was an agent. He put a contract on the table and offered her what she wanted more than anything-to be young again. To have the beauty and skill she once had, to command the respect and admiration she once had, if she just signed on the dotted line. She was so desperate, so hungry for her past lory, she didn't even think to ask the price. She just signed, then and there. They walked out together and he led her away. She wasn't sure how long they walked but eventually he began to lead her through thorns and brambles. They snagged her flesh and sliced her skin, but the man told her it would al go away once she was there. So she kept walking, she suffered the thorns for the promise of her old beauty. And when she emerged at the other side, the Man kept his word.<br /> <br /> He took her away and reshaped her-she can't remember how-and when it was over, she was at least as beautiful as she had been in her prime, perhaps moreso. But then it was time for her to fulfill her end of the bargain. She was set on stage and she was forced to perform, over and over, one play after another, one song after another one dance after another. Her grace and youth were pushed to the edge. She was made to constantly perform for her new master and whatever audience of goblins and creatures he decided to conjure up. When she asked to stop, she was threatened with the taking of her youth, so she went back to performing.<br /> <br /> But eventually, she found her breaking point. Eventually, she reached the end of enough. Her youth and talent had led her to ruin, so what were they really worth? So one evening, when she was on stage, she put everything she had into the performance. She gave the most heartrending, moving performance of her life. It was enough to bring her keeper to tears, sobbing into his hands at the sheer beauty of it. And while the audience wept, she ran from the stage, from the theatre, from Arcadia. She forced her way back through the thorns, not caring about how they snagged her flesh, not stopping until she was safe and home. <br /> <br /> Now she's a darkling, her faith in her old passions and values long shattered. Her skin is etched with the scars of her escape-or possibly of her first visit to Arcadia, she can't be certain-and she looks older now than when she fled Arcadia, though not as old as when she signed her contract. She works in a youth center now, helping troubled kids make something of themselves. She teaches the beautiful young people lessons that are harsh but true, that they need to learn-that youth and beauty aren't virtues. That the world will chew you up if you aren't watchful. And always, always, read the fine print.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:07:31-07:00","id":994590,"title":"","content":"Siobhan Malloy was born to a family of Awakened, but she resented the supernatural world that she had to grow up knowing. It did not help that some part of her was bitter over having parents who were Awakened, and a younger sister singled out by virtue of being a Proximus. Wanting nothing more than a mundane life, she left for another city when she was older. And she struggled to reject the fact that monsters truly did lurk in the shadows. Her denial, however, cost her when she refused to acknowledge her Keeper's existence when she came for her.<br /> <br /> In Arcadia, Siobhan was made into a tree marked with arcane sigils, one cornerstone in the enchantment which shielded her Keeper's realm from the spells of her foes. She was wracked with pain each day as she absorbed and redirected hostile magic, and her mind steadily crumbled against the insane laws of the Arcadian realm. It was only when she fell back to the folktales of her family that she found her means of escape, and in return she made a promise to the Hedge that she would honor humankind's storied past.<br /> <br /> Since her return, the Spelldrinker came to join the Jade Court in Toronto, and spent much of her time collecting and archiving new stories for the <i>sultana</i> to tell. Her prestige soon grew to the point that she was handpicked by the Huangdi to lead a motley of her fellow courtiers to seek out new tales in another city.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> For more information on the Spelldrinker kith, check out the homebrew kiths via my hub.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:21:25-07:00","id":994594,"title":"","content":"That is awesome. Does she still have any plant-like aspects to her Mien? Or is it just the sigils","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:59:36-07:00","id":994688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=994594#post994594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is awesome. Does she still have any plant-like aspects to her Mien? Or is it just the sigils</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she is a Dual Kith Spelldrinker and Woodblood, with the former as her primary Kith (with perhaps a few dots in Potent Kith as well). As for her appearance, she is &quot; a real-life wood nymph, with green moss-like hair and skin with the look and feel of tree bark&quot;. The sigils that were carved into her appear as full body tattoos for her Mask, as described <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=894547#post894547\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I do hope my description of her as a Grimm is apt, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 10-28-2016, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:26:39-07:00","id":994782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=994314#post994314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. A classic Durance, but in a mythical way. What made you decide to make him Wizened instead of a Beast though?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was 1e, he'd absolutely be a Beast, but in 2e Beasts are about breaking societal conventions to escape, while Wizened are about recalling and perfecting one's profession or skills. As a counterpoint, I had a notion for a Beast Artist who's the Changeling version of Banksy. \ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:50:23-07:00","id":994861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=994782#post994782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it was 1e, he'd absolutely be a Beast, but in 2e Beasts are about breaking societal conventions to escape, while Wizened are about recalling and perfecting one's profession or skills. As a counterpoint, I had a notion for a Beast Artist who's the Changeling version of Banksy. \ud83d\ude09</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. I'm guessing he's not as spider-like in Mien as I was imagining, then? Does he have really long, flexible fingers and limbs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T09:33:37-07:00","id":995240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=994590#post994590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siobhan Malloy was born to a family of Awakened, but she resented the supernatural world that she had to grow up knowing. It did not help that some part of her was bitter over having parents who were Awakened, and a younger sister singled out by virtue of being a Proximus. Wanting nothing more than a mundane life, she left for another city when she was older. And she struggled to reject the fact that monsters truly did lurk in the shadows. Her denial, however, cost her when she refused to acknowledge her Keeper's existence when she came for her.<br /> <br /> In Arcadia, Siobhan was made into a tree marked with arcane sigils, one cornerstone in the enchantment which shielded her Keeper's realm from the spells of her foes. She was wracked with pain each day as she absorbed and redirected hostile magic, and her mind steadily crumbled against the insane laws of the Arcadian realm. It was only when she fell back to the folktales of her family that she found her means of escape, and in return she made a promise to the Hedge that she would honor humankind's storied past.<br /> <br /> Since her return, the Spelldrinker came to join the Jade Court in Toronto, and spent much of her time collecting and archiving new stories for the <i>sultana</i> to tell. Her prestige soon grew to the point that she was handpicked by the Huangdi to lead a motley of her fellow courtiers to seek out new tales in another city.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> For more information on the Spelldrinker kith, check out the homebrew kiths via my hub.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hand picked by the Huangdi to find new stories in other cities kind of sounds like the Huangdi is trying to get rid of a potential rival, get them far away from positions of influence as possible. Just a possible plot angle to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:23:25-07:00","id":995274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=995240#post995240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand picked by the Huangdi to find new stories in other cities kind of sounds like the Huangdi is trying to get rid of a potential rival, get them far away from positions of influence as possible. Just a possible plot angle to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is that angle. Still, that also has the potential of backfiring if her exposure to so many different stories marks her as a potential <i>sultana</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T19:55:21-07:00","id":995925,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for your ideas and stories, they've been really cool. One of the reasons I started this thread is because a lot of people seem to have trouble with the Durance, and it's one of the reasons why &quot;the PTSD angle is too limiting&quot; and &quot;but why can't my character have had a happy durance?&quot; questions crop up. Some people interpret the durance as always meaning &quot;you were randomly kidnapped, you were tortured nonstop for a few years, then you escaped&quot;, and they miss the almost infinite diversity you have in creating yours. <br /> <br /> For one thing, the &quot;random abduction&quot; angle isn't the only way to go. I'm especially fond of durances that started with the changeling leaving willingly, at least initially, or having a chance to back out, or being there as a result of a deal. Brit, one of my favorite characters that I've created, went to Arcadia willingly, and probably could have left at any time, and that's why her durance was so painful for her when she thinks back: she did the things she did because, in some level, she wanted to. Other changelings can channel their rage and hatred towards their keepers, but the only person she can really hate is herself. The scariest villains are often the ones who can corrupt people and make them do horrible things without ever forcing or threatening them. Some of the most frightening keeper concepts I've seen were those who specialized in letting their changelings dig their own graves, subtly luring them deeper and deeper and letting them break themselves. <br /> <br /> The &quot;deal with the devil&quot; element is, in my opinion, underused in durances, and there's so much potential there. The Gentry can offer you anything, anything at all. Giving you health or strength or beauty or riches is trivial for them. They can offer you the world and more. They can literally make your dreams come true. (One of my favorite True Fae concepts that I've come up with, who might be connected to Brittany's keeper, were a &quot;royal family&quot; of Fae who abducted children, told them they were the secret heirs to their fantasy kingdom, and then moulded them into cutthroat, backstabbing, ironfisted despots). <br /> <br /> You're a promising boxer whose career was ended by an injury? The Others won't just heal it, they'll make you even better. They'll give you fists that would make Tyson weep. Of course, the contract that you signed without reading the fine print specifies that a copy of you made from frozen meat and iron girders is going to be the one who gets your career, while the real you is stuck in their gladiator pits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:15:08-07:00","id":995962,"title":"","content":"Yeah. And the deal aspect is very much essential to the game. Even the random kidnappings are many times tied to an ancient agreement you broke without knowing by stepping into the wrong area. I did that with the foster kid character I talked about. I wasn't sure the specifics, but my thought was that his Keeper was out Ironside posing as the head of some sort of shelter or other organization set up to help foster kids about to age out of the system, and they would have them actually sign an agreement that said that they consented to their &quot;rehabilition&quot; or &quot;social improvement&quot; program.<br /> <br /> <br /> Off topic, but I like that last example because I'm imagining how hard it would be to beat that fetch in a straight-out brawl. I'm thinking someone who's olympic level or better in pretty much (high end human physical stats) in everything related to boxing. So many cool things you could do with that.<br /> <br /> 1) Make peace with him and get some awesome backup in a fight<br /> <br /> 2) Epic, no-magic boxing duel to the death<br /> <br /> 3) Joining a local boxing league when you get out and unknowingly signing up to proceed to option 2<br /> <br /> 4) Convoluted plan to kill him indirectly<br /> <br /> 5) Trying to sneakily kill him, hampered by the security systems and guards of the mansion he bought with his winnings and endorsement deals.<br /> <br /> The list goes on and on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:35:11-07:00","id":995967,"title":"","content":"One NPC I have went into his durance willingly, the gentry requesting aid for his subjects as his lands had entered an era of darkness, aid that his bright mind possessed could provide on such short notice. Once in Arcadia he quickly discovered that the king was speaking a lot more literally than he expected, the land was literally without light and he was transformed into a grand star aloft in the sky. Admittedly, his light did rejuvenate the kingdom and bring hope for it's subjects (many of which are changelings). But he was flame, and a flame requires fuel, so he was made to constantly try and learn more and more so it didn't dull his light. His child mind couldn't handle constant learning to such a severe degree and eventually he forced his way back to the Ironside.... leaving the kingdom in gloom and despair. He still regrets betraying all those people just for his own sake.<br /> <br /> Bright One Darkling of the Sand Court","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-31-2016, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:45:43-07:00","id":995969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=995967#post995967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One NPC I have went into his durance willingly, the gentry requesting aid for his subjects as his lands had entered an era of darkness, aid that his bright mind possessed could provide on such short notice. Once in Arcadia he quickly discovered that the king was speaking a lot more literally than he expected, the land was literally without light and he was transformed into a grand star aloft in the sky. Admittedly, his light did rejuvenate the kingdom and bring hope for it's subjects (many of which are changelings). But he was flame, and a flame requires fuel, so he was made to constantly try and learn more and more so it didn't dull his light. His child mind couldn't handle constant learning to such a severe degree and eventually he forced his way back to the Ironside.... leaving the kingdom in gloom and despair. He still regrets betraying all those people just for his own sake.<br /> <br /> Bright One Darkling of the Sand Court</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perfect use of dream logic. I love it. So what's the emotion of the Sand Court?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T22:55:49-07:00","id":995974,"title":"","content":"There was a really fascinating NPC faction for the Walking Shadows campaign, where it was a family loyal to a True Fae started by an ancient chinese sorcerer and scientist who &quot;studied&quot; under the Fae and remained loyal to it, and ultimately formed a cult dedicated to it that periodically sent members to Arcadia to &quot;study&quot; under it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T23:48:04-07:00","id":995984,"title":"","content":"I think i remember something like that. Were they involved in organized crime?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T00:35:01-07:00","id":995989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/990737-post-your-durance?p=995969#post995969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perfect use of dream logic. I love it. So what's the emotion of the Sand Court?</div> </div> </div> </div>Excitement, it's a slightly delusional court based on the potential future for the freehold it's in where their is the hope of the freehold to become more of a vacation destination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 10-31-2016, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T17:20:56-07:00","id":996336,"title":"","content":"This is my character's, his name is Victor Cowen<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Victor was captured at the age of 10 by a member of the gentry while he was walking back home from Karate Practice, born a Yank he was living over seas due to his father\u2019s job. The gentry that took him, Count Inderline of the Surtr Hold, had fallen into a recent gentry fad of games of living chess. The Gentry would stand in for the King, and all other pieces started as pawns. Should they cross and get promoted they were allowed to pick their new roles. This particular Gentry had been on a losing streak but when he saw a youth who was skilled with a spear he snapped up the boy as fast as he could. The rules of this game of chess varied from normal with one small difference. They had to actually best the enemy in battle to capture them and if they were defeated they were captured instead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Victor was turned into a pawn and given a the basic gear of his new role, but also given the duty of training the other boys and girls how to fight, since the Count had better things to do. Victor\u2019s strong sense of justice quickly lead him to be respected both as their teacher and as one who would always be by their side. He was well loved by the others both for his handsome face and kind instruction. Yet at other times when they were in danger his wrath would help him in protecting the younger and less experienced pieces. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Soon his team started to do better, though going against more complete teams was still hard. But soon they were putting enemies in check, and Victor fell in love with Charity. One day he hatched a plan and they arranged to drive her forward and she became first pawn among them to be promoted and she became the Queen, and a Fairest Dragon. Charity\u2019s friend Alison became Jealous of her and convinced their keeper that as the queen only he should be her lover. And so they were separated. She coveted Victor and his love for Charity so she stole the opportunity to stand next to the queen and became the queen side Bishop. When Victor got his promotion he became the queenside Knight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alison the Bishop took as her rewards for putting the other gentry into check Victor. The hurt on her friends face made her happy each and every time, for she knew that Charity could not lay her hand upon the burning knight of their set. It made Alison happy. Meanwhile for his reward Victor chose Tyrfring, the blood thirsting sword.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Eventually hey had a full set, and their power was great, as they crashed through foes. Though as the gentry are prone to they grow bored with their entertainments and s the count discarded his chess set but took the kingside pieces and gave them new lives elsewhere. Before they starved to death Charity lead the queen side to escape into the hedge and back to their lives. Victor\u2019s blazing ferocity helped them cut their way through. Then, just when they are nearly through Alison turned on Charity and tore the heart of chest, laughing. She stole a kiss from Victor in the thorns, while he was paralyzed by the death of Charity, and promised to capture him for her own again on the other side.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T19:33:13-07:00","id":996401,"title":"","content":"He was your average guy in South Korea. And just like every adult male born there, the law dictated that he serve the military either as a conscripted soldier or some form of officer in his youth. Knowing very well how anachronistic and repressed the experience of years of mandatory military service are and will be, the man sought a way out. No such luck, though - it's not like he had connections to illegally fake his medical records or assign himself to easier posts, or the guts to wound himself and feign an accident.<br /> <br /> It was then he saw a random flier on the way to his health checkup, something about guaranteed fulfillment and excitement. Oh, what the hell, the man thought, and stepped out of the asphalt road leading to the proper building, and on to some underused road. He really should've read the fine print past all the jargon. It did say experience &quot;unlike anything you'd find in this world.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sleeping and training with men of all shapes and sizes, definitely not Korean. Quarters adorned with classic camouflage patterns, but layered over architecture both modern and medieval, familiar and strange. Equipment and weaponry that for some reason included broadswords and halberds alongside hand cannons and fusiliers, and tower shields alongside kevlar. Training regimens designed to either make a man into a one-man army or let him whimper and die in the half-frozen mud. Marches along mountains crowned with thunderstorms and canyons filled with mists that had something hungering inside them. Five weeks of training had passed - or was it five years? Five days? The man was assigned to a unit within the mountains and forests. Which had frequent skirmishes with armored and armed soldiers equipped strangely as himself and his comrades, even more frequent outbreaks of wild beasts the man was sure that they weren't native to any part of the planet, and nigh continuous labor building new barracks and hoisting of heavy military equipment that he had no idea what they were parts of.<br /> <br /> Twenty-one months had passed, or so the man thought it had. The man just reasoned so because he had seen seven seasons pass by, but never counted how long each one lasted. That winter did last awfully long, though, seeing as how he and his fellow soldiers had to chip away a glacier that formed behind the barracks. The man still remembered that mandatory military service in the ROK Army lasted for twenty one months. So when he went to the commander and talked about release from duty, the elfish officer sent him off to confinement for daring to speak up to him.<br /> <br /> That was the last straw on this naive man who by this time figured out that he was not your normal army. So he decided to break out. He banged on the walls of the guardhouse, the loud warnings of his wardens be damned, screaming profanities and curses. When his fists turned red and blue from bruises, he started to kick. When his feet and knees all broke, he started to throw himself at the concrete. When all of his skin blistered open and the guards finally decided to take him out for his own safety, the walls crumbled down. The man was crushed by the debris and tangled by camouflage veils and his own uniform, but rose up with newfound vigor and started to run. He felt parts of rock and cloth fell off him. Or was that his own flesh and bones? Either way, he rampaged his way out. Guards shot blank ammo at him to subdue him, but he ignored all the pain. He rushed straight through the wires surrounding the barracks, through the thorns of the lush forest beyond the camp, and ended up right back where he took that discourse on the asphalt road.<br /> <br /> An Ogrish Soldier and a Broadback, member of the freehold of Seoul","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}